From 41c184238a2e91403d83ffc34b9e5b73407ae656 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <324514544+sysretq0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: mutex: Defer when mutex device is not probed
 yet

mtk_mutex_get() dereferences dev_get_drvdata(dev) without checking if
the disp-mutex platform device has finished probing. When the display
power domain controller defers (for example waiting for a domain-supply
regulator), mediatek-drm can reach mtk_mutex_get() while the mutex
platform_device exists in DT but its driver has not bound yet, causing a
NULL pointer dereference at offset 0x19 (mtx->mutex[0].claimed).

Return ERR_PTR(-EPROBE_DEFER) if dev_get_drvdata(dev) is NULL.

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <324514544+sysretq0@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-mutex.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-mutex.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-mutex.c
index 6b50dec..d1e2691 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-mutex.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-mutex.c
@@ -872,6 +872,9 @@ struct mtk_mutex *mtk_mutex_get(struct device *dev)
 	struct mtk_mutex_ctx *mtx = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int i;
 
+	if (!mtx)
+		return ERR_PTR(-EPROBE_DEFER);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < MTK_MUTEX_MAX_HANDLES; i++)
 		if (!mtx->mutex[i].claimed) {
 			mtx->mutex[i].claimed = true;
-- 
2.55.0

